# --- env / secrets ---
.env
*.local

# --- editor / tooling local state ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- docs site (Jekyll) build artifacts ---
docs/_site/
docs/.jekyll-cache/
docs/Gemfile.lock
docs/vendor/

# --- reference client installs (excluded) ---
tribes2-unpatched-install-reference/
tribes2-patched-install-reference/

# --- game data (fetched at build time, never via git) ---
# The build no longer needs a game archive: the Dockerfile downloads the public GSI
# installer and extracts GameData from it with REWise (see docs/building-and-deploying.md).
# Any local copy of the old archive stays ignored so it can never be committed (GitHub
# rejects >100 MB files and we don't use Git LFS).
content/tribesinstall.7z

# --- Microsoft VC++ runtime (never vendored; fetched from MS at build time) ---
# Licensing: keep Microsoft binaries out of the repo and its history. The Dockerfile
# downloads the official vc_redist at build time instead. See docs/building-and-deploying.md.
content/vcrun22.zip
